      "content": "I'll read the original test and CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `Value.isEnabled()` returns `false` even after setting `MINIMAL_CLASS` as the id type, because the base `EMPTY` value uses `As.NOTHING` as its inclusion type, which disqualifies it from being \"enabled\". Let me write a clearer version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names (`jsonTypeInfo_Value0`, `jsonTypeInfo_Value1`, `boolean0`) with descriptive names (`emptyValue`, `valueWithMinimalClass`, `enabled`) and adds comments explaining why `isEnabled()` returns `false` despite the id type being `MINIMAL_CLASS`."
